# The Go images copy go.mod, go.sum, the Go sources in this directory,
# and cli/, and nothing else. Everything below is documentation, plans,
# manifests, test data, smoke scripts, generated skills, a workstation's
# build output, or the source of an image with its own context (the
# media browser's Rust tree and Corrosion). Sending any of it to the
# daemon costs the build time and no Go build reads it. A change to any
# of it must not rebuild the Go images, and CI selects images by what
# this file leaves in. The cargo target directory is the large one,
# gigabytes on a workstation.
deploy
docs
plans
testdata
local
media-browser
corrosion
skills
smoke
coverage.out
coverage-media-browser.xml
README.md
LICENSE
/library-operator
